From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dodaskot <pessdres@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 10:26:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 059/131] ASoC: mediatek: mt6359-accdet: add an OF match table

The MFD core creates the device as "mt6359-accdet" with the
mediatek,mt6359-accdet node while the driver is named
"pmic-codec-accdet" and had no OF table, so it never bound.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/mt6359-accdet.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/mt6359-accdet.c b/sound/soc/codecs/mt6359-accdet.c
index ed34cc15b..f4f1a8dcf 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/mt6359-accdet.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/mt6359-accdet.c
@@ -1047,9 +1047,16 @@ static int mt6359_accdet_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	return ret;
 }
 
+static const struct of_device_id mt6359_accdet_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6359-accdet" },
+	{ /* sentinel */ }
+};
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, mt6359_accdet_of_match);
+
 static struct platform_driver mt6359_accdet_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "pmic-codec-accdet",
+		.of_match_table = mt6359_accdet_of_match,
 	},
 	.probe = mt6359_accdet_probe,
 };
